verdict.corrected:
No committed number or pre-registered verdict changes. The write-up (FACTBANK_PLAN_RESULTS.md, not yet written) should add a caveat along these lines.

"v9's 0.975 (and v9n's and v10's) is the pre-registered result. It is also the highest v9 reaches on these 50 questions under any wording we tried.

In a check made after the test, and not pre-registered, we asked the same questions in other wordings, keeping the same documents and expected answers:
- the training wordings and writer 2's wordings alone also give 0.975;
- they miss the same two questions (action_owner_issues-021, ticket_link-status-039), which fail under every wording;
- writer 1's wordings alone give 0.922;
- the unused third blind writer's give 0.872 (v9n 0.843);
- the wordings seen during development give 0.922–0.940.

Only three questions changed with the writer drawn: ticket_link/status 020, 025 and 026. With writer 1's formal wording, v9 answered with an assignee instead of a status. The pre-registered random draw happened to give all three to writer 2, a 1-in-8 chance. Over all writer-1/2 draws v9 averages 0.949 (5–95%: 0.923–0.975).

For v9, then, the test's wordings were no harder than its training wordings. The test does not show that v9 is robust to new wording; a fair expectation on new blind wordings of these kinds is about 0.87–0.95.

Rules 1, 2, 3 and 5 hold under every wording tried. Rule 4's 'not met' does depend on the draw: with writer 1's or writer 3's wordings alone, v10 − v9 would be +0.053 or +0.052, just meeting the bar, and about 12% of writer-1/2 draws would meet it. v9n's tie with v9 also depends on the draw: v9n trails by 0.035 with writer 1's wordings and by 0.029 with writer 3's."

Replace item 6 with: "6. **v4's low score (0.510) means these 50 questions are hard for v4, not that the test is hard.** It does not come from the mix of kinds, which is ordinary: v4's per-kind rates from the five earlier sets predict 0.623 for this mix, against 0.614 to 0.654 for the earlier sets' own mixes. It comes from v4 doing worse within kinds on these particular questions:
- on these documents v4 gets 0 of 3 linked-ticket assignees and 0 of 5 pull-request authors in every wording;
- it gets 0.61 of the action-item lists even in the training wordings;
- its person_first (2/7) and person_count (4/8) losses come from the drawn wording, since both score full marks in the training wordings.
Asked in the same wording as an earlier set, v4 scores 0.10 to 0.20 lower on these questions (0.632 against 0.727, 0.416 against 0.611, 0.488 against 0.586), while v9 does not drop the same way (0.940 against 0.958, 0.923 against 0.877, 0.940 against 0.983). Across the six sets, v4's and v9's scores do not move together (r = -0.12). So v9 - v4 = +0.465 is larger than on the earlier sets (+0.23 to +0.40, mean +0.32) because v4 did badly on these questions, not because they suit v9. Rule 1's verdict does not depend on this: v9 - v4 >= 0.31 in every wording tried."
